            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi DistLattice
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^{op} \to DistLattice
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to the category of distributive lattices is called the
            %strong coherent hyperdoctrine
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#for_a_coherent_theory For a coherent theory
          %p
            Accordingly, there is a coherent hyperdoctrine associated with any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+theory"} coherent theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are lists of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+variables"} free variables
            in the theory, and the lattice assigned to them is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            of the theory in this
            = succeed "." do
